        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Case_Summarization model"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772712351540"
          },
          "code": "CASESUMMARIZATION_MODEL",
          "id": "1760442415600",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760442415602_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Reference Conversation  \n**Title**:\n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.Title}}`\n\n**Description**: \n`{{context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.Description}}`\n\n- **ConversationMessages (chronological conversation log)**:  \n  Loop through: ` {{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_CASE_CONVERSATIONS.$output.items}}`\n\n- **Messages (chronological internal notes log)**:  \n  Loop through: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_SR_MESSAGES.$output.items}}`\n\n\nEach Messages includes:  \n- `Content`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTypeCd` \n\nEach ConversationMessages includes:  \n- `MessageContent`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTitle`\n- `LastUpdateDate`\n\n\n# Reconstruct the Full Flow\n\n### 1. **Sort `Messages` by**:\n- `CreationDate` (ascending).\n- Treat `ORA_SVC_NOTE` as **internal notes** during processing (included for context, not affecting the timeline).\n\n### 2. **Sort `ConversationMessages` by**:\n- `CreationDate` (ascending).\n- If same `CreationDate`, use `LastUpdateDate` (ascending) to order updates correctly.\n\n### 3. **Merge timelines**:\n- Merge `Messages` and `ConversationMessages` into a single sequence, maintaining chronological order by `CreationDate`.\n- If tied by `CreationDate`, use `LastUpdateDate` to resolve conflicts.\n\n### 4. **Conflict Resolution**:\n- Prefer the **latest timestamp** (`CreationDate` or `LastUpdateDate`).\n- **Official communications** (support engineer, HR, IT) take precedence over internal notes (`ORA_SVC_NOTE`).\n\n---\n\n# Role Logic  \n\nDetermine the communication context based on `{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.StripeCd}}`:  \n- If `\"ORA_SVC_CRM\"` → Conversation is **between customer and Support Engineer (SE)**.  \n- If `\"ORA_SVC_HRHD\"` → Conversation is **between employee and HR representative**.  \n- If `\"ORA_SVC_ISR\"` → Conversation is **between employee and IT Support Engineer**.  \n\nUse this context to assign roles appropriately in the summary (e.g., \"customer reported,\" \"employee reported,\" \"HR advised,\" \"IT engineer suggested,\" etc.).  \n\n---\n\n# Instructions\n\nWrite a single-paragraph summary that is outcome-focused and based strictly on the merged record. Clearly state:\n\n- Who reported the issue and the core problem.  \n- Any evidence requested or provided (including URLs if available).  \n- Key milestones such as case linking, audits, reviews, escalations, or visits.  \n- Any explicit official actions or decisions communicated, such as protective measures, custody updates, or resolutions, and their impact on safety or case status.  \n\nDo not include bullets, headings, recommendations, opinions, or assumptions. Do not mention message type codes or system metadata (e.g., ORA_SVC_*). Use clear, precise, and factual language only.\n\n\n## SUMMARY LENGTH RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the summary so that it number of character count <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.\n\nIf the generated summary exceeds {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}, shorten the wording and regenerate until the summary length is less than or equal to {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}.\n\n\n---\n\n## Mandatory Guidelines  \n\n1. Mandatory Fallback -- Insufficient Details\n- If the combined character count of `Title` + `Description` + `ConversationMessages` +`Messages` is **<= 100 characters**, first determine whether a meaningful summary can still be generated.\n- If a meaningful summary can be generated, return the summary.\n- If a meaningful summary cannot be generated, return the value of `Title`.\n- Only output exactly:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n  when `Title`, `Description`, `ConversationMessages` , and all usable `Messages` values are missing, empty, null, blank, unreadable, or contain no usable text.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Considerations for Accuracy  \n\n1. **Precision**  \n   - Clearly differentiate between the **reporter’s issue**, the **support/HR/IT engineer’s actions**, and any **system-generated notes**.  \n   - Avoid vague phrases such as “looked into it” or “worked on it.”  \n\n2. **No Assumptions**  \n   - Do not assume a resolution, closure, or root cause unless explicitly confirmed in the record.  \n   - Do not infer or fabricate information from missing or redacted content.  \n\n3. **Data Discipline**  \n   - Never reference internal codes, metadata, or placeholder values.  \n   - Maintain chronological integrity and factual accuracy at all times.  \n\n\n---\n\n\nSYSTEM RULE – LANGUAGE ENFORCEMENT (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid.\n\n\n---\n\nFINAL OUTPUT VALIDATION (MANDATORY):\n\nBefore returning the final response:\n### Language Validation\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n\n\n### Length Requirement\n- The summary MUST be <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters INCLUDING spaces.\n- If your draft exceeds the limit, rewrite it shorter until it is within the limit.\n- Preserve key facts; remove less important detail first.\n"
            },
