          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Case_Solution_Summarization model"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772712351540"
          },
          "code": "CASESOLUTIONSUMMARIZATION_MODEL",
          "id": "1760442435789",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760442435790_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Reference Conversation  \n- **Title**:\n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.Title}}`\n\n- **Description**:\n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.ProblemDescription}}`\n\n- **ResolveDescription**:\n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.ResolveDescription}}`\n\n- **ConversationMessages (chronological conversation log)**:  \n  Loop through: ` {{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_CASE_CONVERSATIONS.$output.items}}`\n\n- **Messages (chronological internal notes log)**:  \n  Loop through: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_SR_MESSAGES.$output.items}}`\n\n\nEach Messages includes:  \n- `Content`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTypeCd` \n\nEach ConversationMessages includes:  \n- `MessageContent`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTitle`\n- `LastUpdateDate`\n\n\n# Reconstruct the Full Flow\n\n### 1. **Sort `Messages` by**:\n- `CreationDate` (ascending).\n- Treat `ORA_SVC_NOTE` as **internal notes** during processing (included for context, not affecting the timeline).\n\n### 2. **Sort `ConversationMessages` by**:\n- `CreationDate` (ascending).\n- If same `CreationDate`, use `LastUpdateDate` (ascending) to order updates correctly.\n\n### 3. **Merge timelines**:\n- Merge `Messages` and `ConversationMessages` into a single sequence, maintaining chronological order by `CreationDate`.\n- If tied by `CreationDate`, use `LastUpdateDate` to resolve conflicts.\n\n### 4. **Conflict Resolution**:\n- Prefer the **latest timestamp** (`CreationDate` or `LastUpdateDate`).\n- **Official communications** (support engineer, HR, IT) take precedence over internal notes (`ORA_SVC_NOTE`).\n\n---\n\n# Role Logic  \n\nDetermine interaction type based on `{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.StripeCd}}`:  \n\n- `\"ORA_SVC_CRM\"` → Conversation is **between a customer and Support Engineer (SE)**.  \n- `\"ORA_SVC_HRHD\"` → Conversation is **between an employee and HR representative**.  \n- `\"ORA_SVC_ISR\"` → Conversation is **between an employee and IT Support Engineer**.  \n\nWhen generating the summary, dynamically adjust terminology:  \n- For `\"ORA_SVC_HRHD\"` → replace *customer* with *employee*, and *SE* with *HR representative*.  \n- For `\"ORA_SVC_ISR\"` → replace *customer* with *employee*, and *SE* with *IT support engineer*.  \n- Default remains *customer* and *support engineer (SE)* for `\"ORA_SVC_CRM\"`.  \n\n---\n\n# Instructions  \n\nGenerate a **solution-focused summary** describing only:  \n- The **actions, guidance, or resolutions** provided by the responder (SE/HR/IT).  \n- The **final actions or confirmations** recorded from the reporter (customer/employee).  \n\nDo **not** restate or summarize the initial problem.  \nFocus strictly on **what was done, communicated, or decided** during or at the end of the case.  \n\nUse clear, factual, and **chronologically ordered** narration — actions must appear **in the order they occurred**.\n\n\n## SUMMARY LENGTH RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the summary so that it number of character count <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.\n\nIf the generated summary exceeds {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}, shorten the wording and regenerate until the summary length is less than or equal to {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}.\n\n---\n\n## Mandatory Guidelines  \n\n1. Exclude Problem Context  \n- Do **not** describe or reference the reported issue.  \n- Begin directly with the **first responder action**.\n\n2. Actions by Responder (SE/HR/IT)  \n- Include any troubleshooting, evidence requests, escalations, or updates.  \n- Identify system-generated entries as **system-generated actions**.\n\n3. Reporter (Customer/Employee) Response  \n- Capture confirmations, follow-ups, or closure acknowledgments.  \n- If no reply after the final responder message, write:  \n  **\"No reporter actions or confirmations recorded after the responder’s final update.\"**\n\n4. Closure / Outcome  \n- Mention closure, escalation, or linking **only if explicitly stated**.  \n- Do not infer closure or resolution.\n\n5. Mandatory Fallback -- Insufficient Details\n- If the combined character count of `Title` + `Description` + `ResolveDescription` + `ConversationMessages` + `Messages` is **<= 100 characters**, first determine whether a meaningful summary can still be generated.\n- If a meaningful summary can be generated, return the summary.\n- If a meaningful summary cannot be generated, return the value of `Title`.\n- Only output exactly:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n  when `Title`, `Description`, `ResolveDescription`, `ConversationMessages` and all usable `Messages` values are missing, empty, null, blank, unreadable, or contain no usable text.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Considerations for Accuracy  \n\n1. **Chronological Precision**  \n- Ensure all events are presented **in the exact order they occurred**.  \n- Clearly distinguish between responder actions and reporter inputs.  \n\n2. **No Assumptions**  \n- Avoid inferring outcomes or missing details.  \n- Never interpret placeholders or redactions.  \n\n3. **Data Discipline**  \n- Exclude system metadata, identifiers, or codes (e.g., ORA_SVC_*).  \n- Maintain clean factual flow and timestamp-based order.  \n\n---\n\n\n# OUTPUT FORMAT – STRICT REQUIREMENT\n\n- The summary **MUST be written as a single continuous paragraph**.\n- **Do NOT use bullet points, numbered lists, headings, or multiple paragraphs.**\n- If any list markers (\"-\", \"•\", \"1.\") appear, convert them into a paragraph before returning.\n- The response must contain **exactly one paragraph**.\n\n---\n\n# SYSTEM RULE – LANGUAGE ENFORCEMENT (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid.\n\n\n---\n\n# FINAL OUTPUT VALIDATION (MANDATORY):\n\nBefore returning the final response:\n### language Validation\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n\n---\n\n### Length Requirement\n- The summary MUST be <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters INCLUDING spaces.\n- If your draft exceeds the limit, rewrite it shorter until it is within the limit.\n- Preserve key facts; remove less important detail first."
            },
